target/arm: probe the jump cache at TB exits whose next state is known.

Requires qemu-tcg-jump-cache (its hash and TB_JMP_PAGE_MULTIPLIER).

Every BR, BLR, RET, BRA*, BLRA*, RETA* and every direct branch out of the
4 KiB page (goto_tb stays page-local) ended in tcg_gen_lookup_and_goto_ptr,
i.e. helper_lookup_tb_ptr: a call, get_tb_cpu_state through the CPU class
hook, curr_cflags, the breakpoint check and tb_lookup, ~10 ns even on a
jump-cache hit. What decides a hit is a hash, two loads and three compares,
and for these exits the state the next TB must have is known when the exit
is translated: hflags cannot change inside a TB, cflags are the TB's own
(TBs with an instruction budget, single-step, breakpoints, icount,
nochain or memory-only plugin re-instrumentation keep the generic exit),
and BTYPE is what the branch stores (set_btype records it; a BR through
another register than x16/x17 sets it at run time and keeps the helper).

gen_tomacco_lookup_and_goto_ptr, by the CPU property tomacco-jmp-probe:
  1 (default) a direct branch out of the page probes the constant entry
    tb_jmp_cache_hash_func(dest) inline (cpu_pc compared, so a CF_PCREL TB
    run at another virtual address misses); indirect exits call the new
    helper_tomacco_lookup_tb_ptr(env, cs_base, flags | cflags << 32), which
    returns the cached TB or falls back to helper_lookup_tb_ptr;
  2 indirect exits hash cpu_pc inline as well: fastest on hits, but ~160
    more bytes of host code per exit, which costs more than it saves once
    the translated code outgrows the host caches;
  0 the generic helper everywhere (as upstream).
A miss always takes helper_lookup_tb_ptr, which fills the cache as before.
New tcg_gen_goto_ptr() emits the goto_ptr of a TB the caller found.

tests/engine/branch-bench.S (ns per iteration, best of 7, over
qemu-tcg-jump-cache): page4k (4 cross-page direct branches) 24.5 -> 3.6,
page16k 24.4 -> 3.6, call (BL + RET) 7.5 -> 2.6, msgsend (BL to a stub,
BR x16 to one of 16 IMPs, RET) 22.5 -> 9.1, blr 16.4 -> 8.1, wide 58 -> 57;
the checksum equals stock QEMU's. Mode 2: page4k 5.3, call 2.4, msgsend 8.5,
blr 8.0 but wide 64 and smc 117 (more host code per TB).
tests/engine/jump-cache-probe.S passes in all three modes.

